# SOPS / age private keys — never commit a real one (the demo example is kept).
# *.key is deliberately broad: the SOPS README tells you to run `age-keygen -o
# age.key`, and a reader who names theirs prod.key should not be caught out by a
# pattern that only matched the example filename.
*.key
*.agekey
age.key
keys.txt
!deploy/k8s/sops/age-example.key
# real (non-example) sealed secrets stay local unless you intend to commit them
deploy/k8s/sops/secrets.sops.yaml
# Same safety default for the two files Phase 79 added: it stops a HALF-FINISHED
# secrets file being committed before you have confirmed it is sealed. Once
# verify.sh-style checks pass on your own file, commit it with `git add -f` (or
# drop these rules) so GitOps can see it.
deploy/k8s/sops/pg-app.sops.yaml
deploy/helm/pamv1/secrets.sops.yaml

# `go build ./cmd/archgen` writes this at the repo root, and CLAUDE.md tells every
# contributor to run archgen — so without this line the first person to follow the
# instructions commits a 3.7 MB Linux executable. One did (Phase 195, fixed in 201).
/archgen
